{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Events\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiscoveredEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all"},{"text":" lists every one the program links, from every module, so a store or a tracking plan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be built from it with no list to keep: ","type":"text"},{"code":"SegmentStore()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore(database:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" each use it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","}","","DiscoveredEvent.all.map { $0.type.name }","\/\/ [\"ApplicationBackgrounded\", ..., \"SessionStarted\", \"signed_up\"]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct is discovered, wherever it is declared, unless it is generic or nested in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a generic type, as neither can hold the record ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" places in the binary; the macro notes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each one where it is declared. One declared in an extension of a generic type doesn’t compile.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The library’s own events are discovered too: ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionStarted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionEnded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ControlActivated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Application","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" events of ","type":"text"},{"code":"LifecycleTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their modules are linked. An event that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" by hand, without ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", isn’t:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list it beside the discovered ones, ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiscoveredEvent.all.map(\\.type) + [Legacy.self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Limits","anchor":"Limits","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An object file in a static archive that nothing references brings no record into the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"program: the linker leaves it out, the library’s own events’ files included. SwiftPM links","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every object file, and so does Bazel: from rules_swift 3.0, ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift_library","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"alwayslink = True","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" unless a target says otherwise, and rules_swift_package_manager sets it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on every target of a package. Apple’s linker, given ","type":"text"},{"code":"-ObjC","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", also loads each member that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declares a Swift type or a protocol conformance, though not one holding only an extension","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that adds members; every ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declares a struct. A static library or static XCFramework","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"linked without ","type":"text"},{"code":"-ObjC","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or a Bazel library with ","type":"text"},{"code":"alwayslink = False","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on Linux, leaves its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unreferenced events out. Link such a library whole","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"-force_load","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on Apple platforms, ","type":"text"},{"code":"--whole-archive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on Linux) to have its events found.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" holds the events of the images loaded when it is called: the program and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamic libraries it links. A library opened later with ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlopen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" adds its events from then on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A library that loads or unloads while "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is read is either read whole or left out of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that read. On Apple platforms one that dyld adds before the read starts is found; on Linux a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlopen"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dlclose"},{"type":"text","text":" waits for the read, so the library is missed. The next read sees it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlclose","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a library that declares events while the process runs. On Apple platforms","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dyld keeps it mapped and its events are still found. On Linux the loader unmaps it while the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift runtime keeps its types registered, and the process can crash later. Keep plug-ins","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"open, or open them with ","type":"text"},{"code":"RTLD_NODELETE","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A module that declares events, linked into two images, lists each of its events twice, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stores and plans refuse the duplicate. Link each such module into one image.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two events of one name in one linked image, the modules linked statically into one executable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or library, fail to build: ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives each record a symbol named for the event’s name,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which the compiler or the linker refuses to define twice. Separate images are never compared,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a name shared with a dynamic library, a library opened with ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlopen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or a module linked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into two images is found only here, and a store or plan built from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" refuses it. So is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one declared inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"private","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"fileprivate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, whose symbol is local to its file.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events"]]},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiscoveredEvent"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiscoveredEvent"}],"title":"DiscoveredEvent","externalID":"s:6Events15DiscoveredEventV","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Events"}],"symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"fileName":"DiscoveredEvent.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent.swift#L59"}},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/schema","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/type"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DiscoveredEvent\/all"],"generated":true}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event type found in the running program: one declared with "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or one of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library’s own events, with its schema."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/events\/discoveredevent"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Events","anchor":"Events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","doc:\/\/Events\/d